Locale data source:           @source@
Locale data origin:           @origin@
Locale data libc version:     @libc_version@
Locale data license:          GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL)
Locale data Unicode version:  @unicode_version@
Locale data upstream version: @package_version@
Locale data upstream URL:     @package_url@

The only change applied to the locale data files is that the
LC_IDENTIFICATION "revision" string has been rewritten as follows:

  "<original revision>; origin=@origin@; unicode=@unicode_version@; localedata=@libc_version@"

Individual locales can be compiled for the host system with:

  I18NPATH=/@prefix@/share/i18n@@origin@/locales \
    localedef -f @prefix@/share/i18n@@origin@/charmaps/CHARMAP \
              @prefix@/share/i18n@@origin@/locales/LOCALE \
              OUTPUT_LOCALE_PATH

Scripts are provided to do that for all locales.  They may be run with
a --dry-run option to show what they would do, and --help for more
details:

@prefix@/share/i18n@@origin@/compile-locales.sh

  Compiles all locales supported by $origin (except broken C.UTF-8
  locales added ny certain downstream distributions of libc),
  installing them under two output directories:

  Names with modifiers:       @prefix@/lib/locales@@origin@
  Names without modifiers:    @prefix@/lib/locales.@origin@

  The resulting locales can be used in three ways:

  1.  Names with modifiers @@origin@, @glibc@libc_version@,
  @unicode@unicode_version@ modifiers can be made available to libc by
  adding the first path to the LOCPATH environment variable.

  2.  Names without modifiers can be made available to libc, hiding
  system locales of the same name, by adding the second path to
  LOCPATH.

  3.  For an alternative way to find @origin@ locales without setting
  LOCPATH, see select-locales.sh below.

  If DESTDIR is set, it will be prefixed to the install location to
  support the creation of pre-compiled locale packages.  Otherwise the
  script must be run as root (or a user with permission to create
  directories under @prefix@).

@prefix@/share/i18n@@origin@/remove-locales.sh

  Removes the @prefix@/lib/locales@@origin@ and
  @prefix@/lib/locales.@origin@ directories, and all compiled locales they
  contain.

@prefix@/share/i18n@@origin@/select-locales.sh add MODIFIER ...

  where MODIFER is @origin, @glibc or @unicode.  If no modifiers are
  given, the default is @origin @glibc.

  Makes locales from @origin@ available to all program without having
  to set LOCPATH, by creating symlinks.  The exposed locale names have
  @@origin@, @glibc@libc_version@ or @unicode@unicode_version@ modifiers as
  requested.

  If DESTDIR is set, it will be prefixed to the system locale path, to
  support the creation of pre-compiled locale packages.  Otherwise the
  script must be run as root (or a user with permission to create
  symlinks under @system_locale_path@).

@prefix@/share/i18n@@origin@/select-locales.sh remove MODIFIER ...

  where MODIFER is as above.  Removes symlinks created by the "add"
  command.